---
layout: base
title: "Setups — What's my local AI?"
description: "Four machines that clear 20 tok/s, what they run, and roughly what they cost."
specRail: true
---
<main id="main" class="page">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title ds-text-gradient ds-text-gradient--animated">Recommended setups</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">
      Four machines that clear 20 tok/s on our estimate. Each card shows the largest Q4 model that fits without dropping
      below that floor.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="setups-grid">
    {% for card in setup_cards %}
      <article class="setup-card">
        <div class="setup-card-head">
          <h2>{{ card.name }}</h2>
          <span class="setup-kind">{{ card.kind }}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="setup-specs">{{ card.specs }}</p>
        <dl class="setup-list">
          <div>
            <dt>Runs</dt>
            <dd>
              {{ card.model }}
              <span class="setup-model-meta">{{ card.model_vram_gb }} GB Q4</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Speed</dt>
            <dd>{{ card.speed_label }}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Price</dt>
            <dd>
              {{ card.price_label }}
              <span class="setup-price-note">{{ card.price_note }}</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="setup-note">{{ card.note }}</p>
        <div class="setup-card-foot">
          <a class="setup-link" href="{{ card.vendor_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            See at {{ card.vendor_label }}
          </a>
          <span class="setup-checked">checked {{ card.last_checked_label }}</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <p class="setups-note">
    Prices are starting points, not quotes. We do not take affiliate money for these.
    <a href="/">Check what your machine runs</a>.
  </p>
</main>
